# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets response headers.
# Consumed by the assets runtime (never served as a file). Local dev (serve.py)
# does not apply these - they only take effect on the Cloudflare deploy.
#
# Deliberately NO Content-Security-Policy: the app lazy-loads WASM, spawns
# blob/module workers and uses data: URIs, so a CSP needs careful per-renderer
# testing before it can be trusted - adding a wrong one silently breaks viewers.
#
# Caching: only the content-stable fonts get far-future immutable caching. app.js
# and analyser.css keep UNVERSIONED filenames and rely on the service-worker cache
# epoch (VERSION in sw.js) for busting, so they must NOT be immutable-cached at the
# HTTP layer or a deploy would serve stale code.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains

/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
